<resources>
    <!-- Android 12+ draws this app's own SplashScreen window from theme
         attributes rather than the platform's generic fallback icon (UX
         review 2026-09-26, "droidtop's own cold-start splash ... shows the
         same generic green Android-robot placeholder instead of a droidtop
         mark", p2-ux-droidtop-app-icons.md). Leaving these unset lets each
         OS/OEM splash implementation decide how to derive an icon from the
         adaptive icon, and that derivation was observed producing the
         platform's default mascot instead of droidtop's own laptop-and-
         robot mark (mipmap/ic_launcher) on at least one test rig. Setting
         them explicitly removes that guesswork: the real launcher icon and
         its own background colour (ic_launcher_background, #1B2430) render
         every cold start, on every API 31+ device, regardless of how a
         given OS build's automatic derivation behaves.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.DroidTop" parent="Theme.AppCompat.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@mipmap/ic_launcher</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">#1B2430</item>
    </style>
</resources>
